|---|---|---|
| `src/runtime.rs` | +52 −24 (resume) | `collection_pairs`, the Counter/defaultdict/deque helpers, persistent stack trees for deque ends, named-record validation, the thirteen `collections.*` arms, a linear `stack_from_values` deque constructor, and `deque_rebalance`, which splits a non-empty side across both ends instead of reversing the whole remainder. The resume makes `deque_value` build an opaque `Object` and splits `deque_parts` into a trusted object path (cheap shape and budget checks) and an untrusted record path (full `validate_stack_tree` walk), so module deques no longer re-walk every node per operation while hand-written records are still refused node by node |
| `src/stdlib.rs` | +116 −1 | registers the `collections` module, its 13 members, builtin names, signatures and the module table |
| `tests/collections_test.rs` | +91 −6 (resume) | 33 tests, all running the program on both engines and comparing values as data as well as text; the resume adds the opaque-object contract, a malformed-grandchild refusal on the untrusted record path, and a 1,500-item both-ends order test that exercises the trusted path |
| `SPEC.md` | +5 −2 (resume) | documents the missing-key behaviour of Counter and defaultdict, their lookup cost, the `put` spelling, deque ends, named fields and field errors; the resume changes the deque description from an opaque record to an opaque value and states the trusted-object rule |
